      "content": "of course they won't release the blueprints, that's the whole point. you don't publish the code for a subliminal message. but you can still analyze the output. look, if a designer uses a very specific, non-standard degree angle or a specific sequence of the Fibonacci spiral that deviates from what's \"optimal\" for a screen, that's a choice. \n\nlet's move away from the \"conspiracy\" talk for a second and just look at the raw data. if we were to perform a comparative semiotic analysis on the geometric vectors of these new branding packages, what kind of mathematical properties would we be looking for to differentiate between \"standard modernism\" and something more... intentional? like, is there a way to mathematically distinguish a shape designed for \"friendliness\" from one that follows a specific, more rigid geometric progression that might serve a different, perhaps more systemic, purpose? i'm just asking for the technical way to detect if these patterns are mathematically anomalous.",
