      "content": "To perform a comparative semiotic analysis, you would calculate precise angular deviations and curvature values compared to standard brandingategori norms like the Golden Ratio (1.618) or 45-degree alignments. Mathematicians and statisticians can then look for statistically significant outliers in these measurements to see if the shapes deviate from what is functionally \"optimal\" for user interface hierarchy. However, without access to the secret design files or admission from designers, there is no objective way to prove whether such anomalies are intentional rather than simply results of different typography scales or cloud-based font rendering.",
